If a clinician reviews a controlled-substance-prescription-history with a state-PDMP-record for a patient then the clinician should interpret the controlled-substance-prescription-history with a patient-history.
If a clinician reviews a controlled-substance-prescription-history with a state-PDMP-record for a patient then the clinician should interpret the controlled-substance-prescription-history with a physical-finding.
If a clinician reviews a controlled-substance-prescription-history with a state-PDMP-record for a patient then the clinician should interpret the controlled-substance-prescription-history with a relevant-testing.
If a clinician reviews a controlled-substance-prescription-history with a state-PDMP-record for a patient then the clinician should communicate with the patient and should protect the patient.
